This is a derivative work. On top of Google's Nearby Connections and Nearby
Sharing libraries it adds and modifies, among other things:

  - a Qt/QML desktop application (sharing/linux/qml_tray_app),
  - Linux platform implementations and transport changes under
    internal/platform/implementation/linux and sharing/linux, including
    Wi-Fi hotspot interface coexistence and an opt-in "Boost" mode.

The Linux platform support this builds on was originally contributed to Google's
Nearby project by proatgram and vibhavp (https://github.com/google/nearby/pull/2098),
and further developed in https://github.com/kidfromjupiter/nearby.

